message: "If you use or refer to this work, please cite it as below."
title: "MARGPA: Modular AI Runtime Governance Prompting Architecture"
authors:
  - family-names: "Takagi"
    given-names: "Yuki"
    alias: "nazuna-2371"
version: "0.1.0"
date-released: "2026-06-08"
url: "https://github.com/nazuna-2371/margpa"
repository-code: "https://github.com/nazuna-2371/margpa"
license: "CC-BY-SA-4.0"
abstract: >-
  MARGPA is an experimental design framework for combining modular
  runtime governance definitions for AI and LLM behavior. This repository
  publishes MARGD, including ARGD and DAGD, as runtime governance definitions
  intended to support premise preservation, context management, evidence
  separation, uncertainty disclosure, self-audit, repair, re-fixation, and
  governance-state reporting in research, design, review, and long-context
  AI workflows.
keywords:
  - "AI governance"
  - "LLM governance"
  - "runtime governance"
  - "prompting architecture"
  - "prompt engineering"
  - "ARGD"
